whole compilation list.  Observe that for this 
compilation, debug was set off for the most modules.

Some of these warnings exist since long time.  Even if the 
program works correct, it should be improved, so that the 
warning disappears.   (example:  if all code lines where a 
certain variable is used,  is skipped without debug, but 
the code line with the definition of that variable is not 
skipped without debug, then this should be improved) .

This also in order to see quickly such new-added modules 
which produce relevant warnings (and which we currently 
have to search among the many old warnings).


